WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
So in February 2022, I went to the city
of Sylhet in Bangladesh with my friend Luke,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.280
and made a travel vlog exploring
both the rural and urban sides of Sylhet.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.280
So I ended up messing up the audio 
on half the video,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.480
because I was using this new camera,
and ended up never publishing it.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.320
But finally I've managed
to recover a bit of it

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.520
and make a video

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.800
from the footage that I have.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.200
So here's my video from Sylhet,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.000
starting from midway
through the first day of the vlog.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.600
I just realized that for the last,
like 2 hours,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.680
I was filming with my microphone
plugged in the headphone jack.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.920
So, over here we have 
some sugarcane juice.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.400
A very good way to get food poisoning if your 
stomach isn't used to the local food here,

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.600
so I wouldn't recommend it if you're traveling.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.960
Alright, we're heading out of town into..

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.280
the rural area, so we can get back 
to our hotel.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.400
And I can't do this for too long
or I'll hit stuff.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.000
So we get out like one kilometer
from the center of the city,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.920
and we're in the middle
of all the tea gardens

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.160
that this city or this region
of Bangladesh is essentially famous for.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.640
And we have the hill tracts 
with all tea plants.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.120
Earlier when we were coming over here,
we could see the women who were like,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.960
cultivating the tea plants literally carrying it
on top of their heads 

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.440
and, taking it to wherever they need to take it.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.080
Maybe we can get off the CNG 
and, take a closer look.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.200
Alright, so we're basically just getting off the Tuktuk (CNG)
to take a better look at the tea garden itself.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.400
Oh, this is really cool.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.840
This is a pretty sick view.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.840
Get off the street and in like ten meters or like ten seconds,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.600
you're in the middle of a tea garden.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.800
And this is, I think, one of the biggest
tea plantations in South Asia.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.440
This part of the country is definitely famous
for being the center of all tea production.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.440
It's a big part of the economy and the 
livelihoods of people who live in this region.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.400
If you've ever been to South Asia
or Bangladesh, you know that

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.040
cha or chai or tea
is a big deal around here.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.320
That's why there are so many tea plantations.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.320
And it goes, like, all the way to the airport.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.840
And I don't know how much further beyond
that, probably all the way to India.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.360
Alright we’re going to the pool area right now.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.960
- 804.
- Thank you. 

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.120
Is that a Jacuzzi on that side 
by any chance?

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.120
No..

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.400
That would be too good to be true.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.200
It is a bit chilly.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.880
- It is actually a bit cold.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.360
Oh, yeah.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.320
I'm gonna check out the warmer pool.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.640
That looks a lot more murky.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.280
It also says no photos and videos,
but literally, clearly they're not very strict on that.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.880
Yeah. It's like a nice, relaxing pool.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.160
It's got, like, pretty good facilities
for a pool in Bangladesh, I got to say. 

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.680
The hotels I used to go to as a kid growing up

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.480
were..

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.280
nothing like this.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.920
And this is not a 
sponsored video by any means.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.080
We're paying, I think, 

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.080
9000 taka for the room per night.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.200
So that's what? $85 or $80.
It's like split for both of us.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.600
So pretty good deal, I would say.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.440
Alright. It's day two,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.120
and we're gonna head out to the Ratargul swamp.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.240
Okay, to go to the swamp,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.320
it's a bit further out from the city
and from where we're staying.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.920
So we're going to take a CNG to get there.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.800
Alright, so we're on our Tuktuk and we are on the way.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:05.040
And for those of you who missed the last video,
I am with Luke Damant..

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.560
in Bangladesh for the first time. 
- Hello.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.480
So, we basically going through 
a bunch of small rural towns or villages

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.080
on the way to the spot.
This is not exactly..

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.880
in the middle of the city
or close to the city of Sylhet.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.440
So we're not off-roading yet,
but we're definitely off the main road.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.040
- Brother, I think I know you. 

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.480
Me? I am Nadir, yeah.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.560
We just saw some, people like planting rice

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.040
on the side of the street, and rice
is like the main food of Bangladesh.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.360
And Luke had never seen that.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.200
So we just, like, stopped 
to get a closer look.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.960
But you see this gentleman behind me
here, planting rice in, like, muddy fields

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.840
and this is how our whole country eats.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.480
Actually, our whole subcontinent
probably eats this more than anything.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.440
For everyone that's not from Bangladesh 
or this region..

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.040
they basically plant..

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.680
these, rice plants on the muddy ground.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.840
And then even if this gets flooded,
They still grow on top of the water.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.800
And in about two months,
they'll be ready to be cultivated

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.000
and for rice to be there.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.520
I met someone from Dhaka as well
who like..

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:02.960
- Nadir On The Go channel.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.600
who recognized me from like 
the other side of the street

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.000
and was like, ‘Oh, you're here.’

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.840
And he's like showing us everything.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.800
My friend Luke the farmer,
planting some rice paddy.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.600
- Oh, it's getting deeper and deeper.
(laughs)

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.320
So I'm going to try to, plant one rice (plant)
without getting too far in the mud,

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.240
because I'm wearing shoes
and I don't want to get my feet too muddy.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.440
- That one’s gonna grow the highest.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:29.560
I think that will work.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.680
I'm officially a farmer.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.680
Mad respect to these guys for doing it.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.280
How old are you?
- I am 15.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.520
He is 15.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.160
He planted all of this since yesterday,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.080
and that's a lot.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.960
You know, it doesn't look like a lot
when he's doing it.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.880
And he's doing so fast.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.200
But there's a technique to it.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.360
There's a skill to it that you need to perfect.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.120
The gentleman who owns the farm, I guess,

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.760
just invited us inside for a cup of tea.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.200
So Luke and I are going
inside for some cha.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:54.520
Uhh.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.080
It’s loud.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.920
So you see people here like straightening out iron

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.960
for a house that they're building over here basically.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.480
They just brought us into the kitchen,

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.680
which is kind of like
under construction outside right now.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.560
And they're making our tea for us right here.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.280
 They’re saying I should wash my hands
cause it's all, like,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.200
muddy from planting that one plant.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.160
I think I broke this.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.640
There’s this little kid here, 
who’s like super shy.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.800
- Name is Nafsan.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.080
- My name is Nafsan.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.080
Aww he is so shy.
- Ask him ‘How are you, uncle?’

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.880
I think he is feeling shy.
(laughs)

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.040
So, the host was kind enough to bring us

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.760
this thing which is called Boroi in Bangla.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.360
I had to look up what it's called in English.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.120
I think it's Chinese date.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.760
And they give it with like salt and chili.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.080
- Oh, there's a seed in there.
Yeah. So don't bite too hard.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:38.600
- Alright.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.200
- It's so sour.
(laughs)

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.800
Okay, I'm going to try one.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.360
Oh, it’s very sour but..
- Yeah.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.480
Umm.. Yeah.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:58.680
I put too much salt on mine to like,
you know, counteract the sourness.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.160
- Trying to grab a mixture. 
Yeah, yeah. Like, have a bit of it.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.640
- Oh it smells nice.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.560
Yeah. It's good.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.920
- It's kind of like the stuff that we had. 
Jhalmuri?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.160
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Jhalmuri, yeah.
Jhalmuri has a bit of this.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:08.800
Cheers.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:13.560
Really nice.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:17.360
That's the beauty of having tea in Sylhet.
It's like locally produced.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.760
- Shoot him. Shoot him. Shoot him.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.880
- (laughs)

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:24.960
- Uncle. Uncle.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:25.720
Weeee

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.760
Solid pitstop.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:31.640
Now we're off to the swamps
where we're originally trying to go.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.000
This part is tricky, actually.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.520
- You need to take a round trip boat from here. Yeah.
Boat to Ratargul?

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.680
So we're getting an engine boat to this spot,

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.760
and then we have to get tickets and go inside.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.480
So it's like 1200 taka, 
which is like $11 to get to the spot

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:46.840
and then, like, tickets.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.920
Here's the weird part. 
It's 50 taka for me, which is like $0.50.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.680
and it's like 500 taka for him or 575,
which is like five and a half bucks.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.240
- I'm Bengali.
(laughs)

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.200
Getting on the boat right now.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.680
This is wobbly.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.200
And we're off.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.240
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.520
So this is why the only pair
of shoes I travel with are hiking shoes.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:27.640
Because, I thought I was coming to a city,
but now I'm, like, climbing these

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:32.200
mud banks, and the hiking shoes
come pretty handy in situations like this.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:37.000
- You don’t need to pay 75 taka, neither 60 taka.
Final price is 500 Taka.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.720
Not clear. What would be the 
final price for two of us?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.760
- 500 Taka for both of you.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.840
500 Taka for both?
- Yeah.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:41.800
Okay. He's giving us a discount.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.120
- Aah.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.880
(Local dialect of Sylhet)

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.520
He's like, giving us a discount.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:48.800
He’s being nice.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.040
- From your country?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:52.440
- Thank you.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.840
We are getting into the forest, 
like the jungle literally.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.520
We’re just surrounded in green, all of a sudden.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.560
I think the swamp is going to be 
a bit ahead of us.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.920
Are you guys coming with us?

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.120
- Yes.
Okay.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.000
So we have two guides 
coming with us for this thing.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.880
So it's very official.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.000
It's not like you just walk into a jungle
and just go for a walk.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.200
There's ticket counters the whole way.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.040
They seem to have a legit process.
And the prices..

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.800
I don't think they're trying to charge us
extra or anything,

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.840
because they lined up with
exactly what the other place said.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.840
I did meet some locals getting on a boat
who told me it would cost the same thing.

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.800
How are you?
- I am fine.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.600
What’s your name?

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.360
- Shahidul Islam.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.120
- This is included with the.. 
I think so.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.880
This is included with the tickets, isn’t it?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.200
Getting on another boat.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.920
Oh, this one's like..
This one's more bouncy. Okay.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.320
Oh, boy.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.000
Alright.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.560
So, I think you want to face the other way maybe.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.560
Now we're in the swamp.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.280
You’ll be in the video.
(laughs)

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:49.320
You’ll see this on internet.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:50.480
- Wow.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:56.960
- (Bangla song)

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.600
So, we have our oarsmen
or the captain of the ship,

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.640
and I don't know the term exactly,
but he's a controlling the boat from this,

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.000
like, little point perched up in the back
where I wouldn't trust my balance

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.280
if I were to sit back there.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.040
And they are singing, which is
like a classic Bangladeshi thing to do.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.520
‘Majhi’ is what we call it,
like the person who's controlling the boat.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.720
They usually are singing
when they're doing their job.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.040
It's like a beautiful thing.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:28.040
- (Bangla song)

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.000
We hit a branch.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.960
We just hit a tree.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:42.960
- (Bangla song)

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.360
- Alright.

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:45.720
We just have to run up?

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:46.720
I think, he's like, run with me.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.520
- Oh. 
Oh man.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.200
That’s gonna be hard to do 
with the camera for sure.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.000
- Be careful. Careful.
Can you film?

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.040
- Hey, can you grab my camera bro?

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:58.680
Yeah.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.520
I got you.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.280
- You may get off.
Let me hold it.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.760
That was quite the adventure.
(laughs)

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.040
- Just for only three minutes.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:10.840
Three minutes. Okay.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.280
It is definitely a good viewpoint,
but we can only be here for three minutes.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:15.560
- It is beautiful.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.560
It's crazy. I've like,

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.160
lived in Bangladesh my whole life, but
I've never even seen a swamp like this.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.320
And I definitely haven't taken a boat across one

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:27.080
And I definitely haven't climbed a fence
to come up to a tower ever in Bangladesh.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.600
But this is gorgeous.
- We didn't even insist.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.760
- He insisted on it. Like..

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:33.640
Yeah, he was like, turn the boat around.
I’m like.. we're like, okay.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.720
- Look at the picture of Ratargul swamp forest.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.600
Yeah. It's beautiful.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.560
Thank you for bringing us.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:38.800
There’s like cobwebs here.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.840
So you know that, like,
not a lot of people come up here.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.280
So the parkour action continued
and these are official guides.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.200
So I guess they knew 
the official rules are better than we did.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.640
- Yeah, come down slowly.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.560
- We don’t have to rush.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:53.840
Do you want me to get the camera?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.040
Yeah this is like.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.520
interesting view down here.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.440
- Oh please let me help.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:00.960
- You can give me that.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.560
So this whole swamp area
is bigger than I thought.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.040
It's 974 acres.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:07.720
This is so gorgeous.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:09.280
So pretty.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.560
So, this is our guide.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.720
But he's also like the tourist
police. He's here to protect us.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:13.680
He's like our security.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.160
(loud whistle)

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.720
Oh, that was loud.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.000
Yeah, that's like our police 
or tourist police guard.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.640
They are saying that all these trees around us
actually go underwater

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:26.440
for six months of the year from the 
River Meghalaya, which is like nearby.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.120
The water overflows and just like 
comes over this whole spot.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.080
We’re back to the riverbank.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.120
And apparently, when it's rainy enough,
you can just take one boat

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.320
from the beginning
all the way into the swamp.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.080
That's what they're saying.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.680
But not right now,
because it's the dry season.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:38.960
- You have to be really careful.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:43.320
In Bangladeshi boats,
you gotta like..

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.160
take the water out with a bucket
so the boat's not sinking.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.240
So that's what he was doing.

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.680
Quite a bit of smoke!

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:02.960
People are just bathing themselves.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.040
We haven't seen a crocodile yet, but
we saw someone, like bathing their cow

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:07.160
and the cow running away.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.520
- It’s gonna hit for sure.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.000
Oh, he knows what he's doing.
- Yeah.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.680
- Finesse it takes to like, not topple
your boat over, must be wild.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:17.800
Teamwork makes the dream work.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.240
- Apparently not. He told me to stop.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.440
Oh really?
(laughs)

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.720
Alright I think we're done for the boat adventures

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.880
So we're back on the road again
towards more civilization.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.600
I am paying him 1300 Taka.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:31.800
Is it okay?

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.960
So, for the CNG or Tuktuk ride,

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.560
we gave him 1300 Taka.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.360
He asked for 800 Taka,
but he stopped so many times.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.800
It's only fair that we give him some extra.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:42.240
It was 1200 for the motorboat
to get to the spot.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.920
Then it was like
50 for me and lot for him,

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:47.720
but they ended up giving us 
a discount. It was like 500 total.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:51.080
And then we like,
tipped them 500 each so like 1500 more.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.320
So I think everything combined was like..

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.480
4000 Taka or something like that?
- Yeah.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:57.200
It was something like 4000 - 4500 Taka.
But you could do it for cheaper.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.000
And if you do it with a bigger group, like,
you know, you can split all those costs.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.760
So like the different boats and stuff.
So it's not going to be as expensive.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.880
But we got really good service,
so we tipped.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.160
This is our hotel that we're staying in.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:10.080
It's costing like, 9000 Taka a night.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:13.080
We also booked last minute
because we accidentally booked, like,

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.120
for the next month.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.360
And we realized when you showed up at
the counter like, oh, it's the wrong booking..

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.640
So that's not bad.
With all the facilities.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.600
Pretty good deal I would say for Bangladesh.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.880
So we're in all this traffic

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:25.760
in the middle of nowhere
because this, this politician, is

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.560
sort of holding a rally
and just going through and there's, like,

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.480
hundreds of motorbikes around him
of his supporters

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.840
going right next to him
in motorbikes and cars.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:37.440
It's crazy, but we found, like,
fans who were on the bike next to us.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.880
They're fans of me and Luke.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.200
Like, they saw his videos in Pakistan.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.200
- How long are you guys staying?
We are leaving tomorrow morning.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.320
- Tomorrow morning?
Yeah.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.880
And to be clear, 
we're not part of this rally.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:50.280
We're just on the road, on a vehicle
while this rally is happening.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:54.000
Alright. We're at the main river in Sylhet.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.360
Which is basically like the Surma river..

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.880
that goes through the 
middle of downtown Sylhet.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.000
And there's, like, this huge bridge
that sort of goes on top of it,

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.520
which is really skinny for being
probably the main bridge of Sylhet.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:10.280
But I think all of this, including the clock, 
has been around since like colonial times.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.120
So this is pretty old stuff.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.160
Interesting thing about this is like this
river, it's not exactly clean.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.000
There's like trash on the side,
but this is..

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.480
way way cleaner than the Buriganga in Dhaka
where we were at a couple of days ago.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:23.720
And you had a goat, right?

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.240
- I bought a goat in Pakistan.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.800
Are you like two-timing on your goat now?
(laughs)

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.640
We’re down at the very base of the river,

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:31.880
where this gentleman is washing 
his legs and feet basically.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.640
And you could technically get a boat
to go somewhere, but I don't think

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.200
we have time for that today.
There's a lot more stuff we want to do.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.360
Oooh

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.120
- How clean.

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.560
- Wow, that is so clean.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.120
I don't know what the name 
of this thing is, but it's called, like,

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.640
tornado potatoes in some places.
And he, like, 

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.680
sliced up the potatoes,
like, spread it out.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.760
And now he's frying it,

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.560
